---
title: The Lakeside Inn's Au Gratin Potatoes
description: Potatoes baked ahead, then simmered in half-and-half for an hour or more before garlic crouton crumbs go on.
tags: [auntie-jeanie]
course: side
icons: [potato, cheese, pan-food]
cuisine: American
source: The Lakeside Inn
servings: 4
---

Bake the @potatoes{1 1/2-2%lb}(680 to 900 g) for ~bake{1%hour}. Let them cool, then peel and cut into 1/2-inch cubes.

Line a 10-inch ovenproof #skillet{} with the potato cubes. Fill it level, and do not pile the cubes on top of one another.

Melt the @margarine{2%tbsp} in a #medium saucepan{}. Add the @half-and-half{1/4%cup}(59 ml), a dash of @salt{1%dash}, and a dash of @white pepper{1%dash}, and blend well. Pour over the potatoes.

Simmer on top of the stove for ~simmer{1-1 1/2%hours}, stirring frequently. Be very careful not to let the pan boil over or overflow.

When done, lightly dust the top with the @Parmesan cheese{1/4%cup}(grated, or an amount to coat the pan).

Mix the @cheese and garlic croutons{1/2%cup}(ground fine) with the additional @&margarine{2%tbsp}, melted, to make the crumbs moist. Spread on top.

Brown in the oven at 350°F (175°C) for about ~brown{10%minutes}.

> **Where It's From** — The Lakeside Inn in Wilbraham, Massachusetts, shared this recipe with a Springfield-area newspaper. Auntie Jeanie clipped it and made it for the family for years.
